><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q5b: sample size power calculation was found suggesting "</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Partial least squares SEM uses an iterative approach&#xD;to analysing the data, and, therefore, it is suggested&#xD;that the sample size should be greater than 10 times&#xD;the maximum number of inner or outer model links&#xD;pointing at any latent variable in the model to achieve&#xD;reliable results".</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
